  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with PCA (config_001) achieves 0.485 accuracy while image-only with ResNet50 (config_010) is far weaker at 0.208, establishing RNA as the dominant modality. The key uncertainty is whether the simple linear PCA encoder is a bottleneck or whether a powerful pre-trained single-cell encoder (scGPT) can substantially improve representation quality. This experiment (config_007: RNA-only, single profile, scGPT) isolates the encoder effect while holding profile setting constant at single profile, directly comparing a learned generative pre-trained representation against PCA. If scGPT significantly exceeds 0.485, it justifies investing remaining budget in scGPT-based multimodal and multiprofile configurations; if it does not, PCA is sufficient and we should pivot to testing aggregation/multiprofile or multimodal fusion. With 7 experiments remaining, resolving the encoder question early maximizes information for subsequent choices."
